From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 15:31:33 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: isp: report and propagate sensor tuning
 failures

NV12 setup ignored every setfile error except EINTR, including a bad
header, a short file and a rejected firmware upload. This made an
unusable tuning file look like a stream running with model tuning.

Keep absent tuning optional, but fail setup for other read, validation
and upload errors. Log failed uploads and add a debug message for a
successful upload. Exercise failure propagation and missing-file fallback
at the capture setup boundary with KUnit static stubs.

Distinguish model-wide sensor setfiles from per-module iCCl factory data
in Kconfig and document the existing NR commands, P010 omissions and the
unimplemented factory calibration/ANE interfaces. Do not change the
qualified preview sequence or guess undocumented firmware parameters.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(backported from commit 64357f8873ad1221d3bc98e89a0455235cf59b94)
